-- The defect gamma fixes, broadcast half (ex36 under old §11 semantics): the scoped-global fold is one scalar, scattered into every pen. Twin of 36-global-vs-gamma.bqn.
-- Same world as 36-farm-gamma-a: rows 0-6 the animals, rows 7-10 the pens. The .bqn old line `#/ (livestock & Cattle)` is not a statement of the fixed language (an un-ticked set-valued relationship is no mask); the broadcast it denoted is the legitimate scoped-global fold #/ (Cattle) — one scalar, 5, broadcast under the Pen mask. The split is lexical: no tick, no @, one scalar.
--! registry 36-farm-gamma-a
--! out 5
--! expect headcount = -1 -1 -1 -1 -1 -1 -1 5 5 5 5

#/ (Cattle)                       -- the scoped-global fold: always one scalar
Pen , Headcount = #/ (Cattle)     -- scalar RHS broadcast into every selected pen: the old defective read
